      children: "While human oversight is essential for high-stakes decisions, relying solely on HITL creates scalability bottlenecks and introduces human error risk. Automated guardrails provide always-on, deterministic protection that operates at machine speed. These fall into three categories: input validation, execution constraints, and output verification. Each layer catches different classes of failures, creating defense in depth that doesn't depend on perfect agent behavior or human vigilance."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
