    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Think of agentic governance like air traffic control. Pilots (agents) have autonomy to fly their planes, but they don't have unrestricted access to airspace. The control tower (orchestrator) coordinates all movements, enforces separation rules (policies), requires explicit approval for critical maneuvers (HITL), and maintains detailed logs of every flight (audit). Pilots are skilled and trusted, but the system doesn't rely on trust alone-structural controls prevent collisions even if a pilot makes a mistake or acts maliciously."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
